        <mxCell id="catalogue-right" value="&lt;b&gt;8  Duplicate side effects&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notifier degraded (sev2)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;9  Tenant mis-attribution&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Attribution mismatch (sev1)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;10  Connect worker loss&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Rebalances, spot evictions, repair throttling (sev3)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;11  Shared-worker blast radius&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partial fleet outage (sev1)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;12  Kafka broker loss at build scale&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fleet stream outage (sev1)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;13  Offset or schema-history topic loss&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Internal topic loss (sev1)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Catalogue exception&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;FM2 follows the suppression rule. FM4 lists every matching alert because the catalogue assigns two severities." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=11;" parent="1" vertex="1">
